<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kiel</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kiel is a port city on the Baltic coast of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and was the principal base of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/german-empire">German Empire</a>'s navy. Its harbour and the Kiel Canal gave it strategic importance. In 1918 a mutiny of sailors at Kiel sparked the revolution that brought down the German Empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kiel.jpg" alt="Kiel" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Diego Delso · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ayuntamiento,_Kiel,_Alemania,_2019-09-10,_DD_96-98_HDR.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
